      "prose": "The line $y = x + k$ is a tangent to the parabola $y = x^2 + 3$.",
      "question": "What is $k$? Give a decimal.",
      "widget": {
        "kind": "numeric",
        "answer": 2.75,
        "tol": {
          "abs": 0.001
        },
        "label": "k",
        "accept": "2.75, or 11/4",
        "wrong": [
          {
            "id": "sign",
            "value": 3.25,
            "tol": {
              "abs": 0.001
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "negative",
            "value": -2.75,
            "tol": {
              "abs": 0.001
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "feedback": {
        "correct": "$x^2 - x + 3 - k = 0$ has discriminant $4k - 11$, which is 0 at $k = 2.75$.",
        "generic": "Not quite right. Set $x^2 + 3 = x + k$, rearrange, and make the discriminant 0.",
        "byKey": {
          "sign": "You wrote the discriminant as $1 + 4(3 - k)$. It is $1 - 4(3 - k) = 4k - 11$.",
          "negative": "$4k - 11 = 0$ gives a positive $k$: $\\tfrac{11}{4}$."
        }
      },
      "explain": {
        "text": "$x^2 - x + (3 - k) = 0$ has discriminant $1 - 4(3 - k) = 4k - 11$. Setting it to 0 gives $k = \\tfrac{11}{4} = 2.75$. The line then touches at $x = \\tfrac{1}{2}$."
      }
